00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:46.510
about moving from every area
is a problem to the mindset

00:02:46.510 --> 00:02:47.882
of failure is normal?

00:02:47.882 --> 00:02:49.840
DAVE RENSIN: A big problem
is that for so long,

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:52.480
we've all been living under
the tyranny of perfection.

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:53.850
We expect perfection.

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:55.570
And I would say to
customers, tell me

00:02:55.570 --> 00:02:57.820
one system designed by humans.

00:02:57.820 --> 00:03:01.100
Software, hardware, economic,
political, anything you want,

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:03.055
that's ever been 100% reliable.

00:03:03.055 --> 00:03:03.680
And they can't.

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:05.010
And you know why they can't?

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:07.570
Because nature has
never built one either.

00:03:07.570 --> 00:03:10.540
So once you accept that
it's not possible to do,

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:13.840
then the question becomes, well,
how much failure is acceptable?

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:15.370
Because you're
going to have some.

00:03:15.370 --> 00:03:17.495
And that's where then we
get into the conversations

00:03:17.495 --> 00:03:19.000
about error budgets and SLOs.

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:20.820
